1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,867
This is Namma Metro Twin,

2
00:00:02,887 --> 00:00:07,657
a 3D digital twin of Bengaluru's
metro that runs right in your browser.

3
00:00:07,677 --> 00:00:09,849
Here's a quick walkthrough.

4
00:00:10,399 --> 00:00:12,261
The map shows the whole network.

5
00:00:12,281 --> 00:00:15,377
The Purple, Green and Yellow
lines are running today.

6
00:00:15,397 --> 00:00:19,922
The Pink and Blue lines are still
being built, so they're drawn dashed.

7
00:00:20,472 --> 00:00:25,018
Every train you see is placed
using BMRCL's published timetable,

8
00:00:25,038 --> 00:00:27,658
matched to the current time in India.

9
00:00:27,678 --> 00:00:33,665
There's no public live feed, so positions
come from the schedule, not from GPS.

10
00:00:34,215 --> 00:00:38,079
Up close, each train is a six-car
model painted in its line colour,

11
00:00:38,099 --> 00:00:42,970
running on the viaducts and through the
tunnels at the real station positions.

12
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:47,387
Above each station, a board shows
the next trains in each direction,

13
00:00:47,407 --> 00:00:49,758
and how many minutes away they are.

14
00:00:50,308 --> 00:00:52,444
Click a station to see its details.

15
00:00:52,464 --> 00:00:57,250
From here you can fly to it, or set
it as the start or end of a journey.

16
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:01,063
The planner finds the route,
including any line changes,

17
00:01:01,083 --> 00:01:04,657
and times it against the
actual trips in the timetable.

18
00:01:05,207 --> 00:01:09,241
Ride mode puts you in the driver's
view of a real scheduled trip,

19
00:01:09,261 --> 00:01:11,237
with next-station announcements.

20
00:01:11,257 --> 00:01:14,538
There's also a VR view
for headsets and phones.

21
00:01:15,088 --> 00:01:16,490
X-ray hides the buildings,

22
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:20,579
so you can see the underground
sections and where the tunnels start.

23
00:01:21,129 --> 00:01:25,835
You can scrub the clock or speed it up,
and the lighting follows the time of day,

24
00:01:25,855 --> 00:01:27,118
from morning to night.

25
00:01:27,138 --> 00:01:29,180
You can add haze or rain too.

26
00:01:29,730 --> 00:01:33,681
Outside the metro area, the map
is covered and marked coming soon,

27
00:01:33,701 --> 00:01:36,096
so the focus stays on the network.

28
00:01:36,646 --> 00:01:41,794
It's built with Mapbox for the
3D city, three.js for the metro,

29
00:01:41,814 --> 00:01:45,814
the open BMRCL timetable
data, and OpenStreetMap.

30
00:01:45,834 --> 00:01:48,357
Credits are in the About panel.

31
00:01:48,377 --> 00:01:51,844
Try it at namma-metro-twin.netlify.app
